    {
      "id": "6a532f68-1d87-4acf-9397-5707993f78d2",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        880,
        -464
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 864,
        "content": "## Employee Timesheet & Overtime Compliance Checker\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs every Sunday evening to review employee timesheet data from Google Sheets. It summarizes hours by employee, calculates overtime/compliance status, then branches between flagged overtime cases and compliant records. Flagged cases are analyzed by an AI escalation agent, emailed to the appropriate manager, and logged separately, while compliant cases are formatted and logged as approved.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the schedule trigger for the desired weekly review time and timezone.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and select the source timesheet sheet plus the destination sheets for flagged and compliant log entries.\n- Ensure the timesheet data includes the fields used by the workflow, such as employee name, employee email, manager email, department, total hours, and overtime hours.\n- Configure Gmail credentials and verify the escalation email recipients, subject, and body content.\n- Configure the OpenAI chat model credentials or local test model settings used by the escalation agent.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the overtime threshold, branching conditions, AI escalation prompt, email template, and logging columns to match company policy and local labor rules."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5dea43f4-d3e2-41fe-8780-69614e01b279",
